title: Controls
intro: Every input action in one window: press a key to bind it, see clashes, and try it in the running game.
project: Platformer | Controls Tour

chapter: One place for the controls | Game > Controls...
say: Until now, changing a game's controls meant writing code. Now there's a window for it.
menu: Game > Controls...
controls
explain: controls:actions | Actions | On the left is every action the game has, with the keys and buttons that do it.
explain: controls:builtin | Built in | These come with Griff, because its components use them.
explain: controls:usedby | Used by | Each one says what uses it. Platformer Movement jumps with Jump, so changing Jump changes how the player jumps.
explain: controls:keys | Keyboard and mouse | Its keys and mouse buttons are here.
explain: controls:pads | Gamepad | And its controller buttons are here.
explain: controls:move | Moving | Moving around always uses WASD, the arrow keys, the D-pad and the left stick.

chapter: Bind by pressing | Press a Key, then the key
action: Jump
say: Lots of players like to jump with W. To add it, click Press a Key, then press W.
bind: W
explain: controls:chip:W | Added | W now jumps, alongside Space.
explain: controls:action:Jump | Changed | The list marks Jump as changed, and Reset to Default puts it back.
bind: X
explain: controls:chip:X | A clash | Here's X too. The window warns that X already does Attack, so pressing it would jump and swing at once.
click: controls:remove:X
say: The cross takes it off again.
bindpad: LB
explain: controls:chip:LB | Gamepad | Controller buttons are picked from a list, so no controller is needed. Now the left bumper jumps too.
expectcontrol: Jump = W
explain: controls:status | Saved as you go | There's no save button. Every change goes into the project file straight away, and exported games use it.
click: controls:close

chapter: Try it in the running game | No restart needed
play
wait: 1
tap: W
wait: 1
say: W jumps.
menu: Game > Controls...
controls
action: Jump
say: The window works while the game runs. Let's take Space off Jump.
click: controls:remove:Space
explain: controls:status | Live | The running game picks the change up at once.
click: controls:close
tap: Space
wait: 1
say: Space does nothing now.
tap: W
wait: 1
say: And W still jumps.
stop

chapter: Your own actions | Add Action
menu: Game > Controls...
controls
click: controls:addaction
say: A game can have actions of its own. Let's add a shield.
actionname: Shield
bind: Q
bindpad: RB
expectcontrol: Shield = Q
explain: controls:usedby | Prompts too | Button prompts and Rebind buttons on a controls screen work with it, just like Griff's own actions.
explain: controls:code | In scripts | And this is the line a script uses to read it. You can copy it straight from here.
click: controls:close
code: project.griff | project.griff
say: It's all kept in the project file, in plain words that read well in git. Only what you changed is written down.
hidecode
